        <PAGEOBJECT XPOS="113.5008" YPOS="1369.375" OwnPage="1" ItemID="172814320" PTYPE="2" WIDTH="337.584" HEIGHT="261.989" FRTYPE="0" CLIPEDIT="1" PWIDTH="1" PCOLOR2="Black" PLINEART="1" LOCALSCX="1" LOCALSCY="1" LOCALX="-782.499999999999" LOCALY="-261.25" LOCALROT="0" PICART="1" SCALETYPE="1" RATIO="1" PRFILE="sRGB display profile (ICC v2.2)" IRENDER="0" path="M0 0 L337.584 0 L337.584 261.989 L0 261.989 L0 0 Z" copath="M0 0 L337.582 0 L337.582 261.991 L0 261.991 L0 0 Z" ImageRes="2" gXpos="113.5008" gYpos="1369.375" gWidth="285.744" gHeight="214.145" GRExtM="3" GRTYPM="2" GRSTARTXM="0" GRSTARTYM="0" GRENDXM="327.650925168442" GRENDYM="0" GRFOCALXM="0" GRFOCALYM="0" GRSCALEM="1" GRSKEWM="0" LAYER="0" NEXTITEM="-1" BACKITEM="-1">
            <M_CSTOP RAMP="0" NAME="Black" SHADE="100" TRANS="1"/>
            <M_CSTOP RAMP="1" NAME="Black" SHADE="100" TRANS="1"/>
        </PAGEOBJECT>
        <PAGEOBJECT XPOS="406.8062" YPOS="928.3798" OwnPage="1" ItemID="172824784" PTYPE="4" WIDTH="292.3813" HEIGHT="440.8702" FRTYPE="0" CLIPEDIT="0" PWIDTH="1" PLINEART="1" LOCALSCX="1" LOCALSCY="1" LOCALX="0" LOCALY="0" LOCALROT="0" PICART="1" SCALETYPE="1" RATIO="1" COLUMNS="2" COLGAP="7.2" AUTOTEXT="0" EXTRA="0" TEXTRA="0" BEXTRA="0" REXTRA="0" VAlign="0" FLOP="1" PLTSHOW="0" BASEOF="0" textPathType="0" textPathFlipped="0" path="M0 0 L292.381 0 L292.381 440.87 L0 440.87 L0 0 Z" copath="M0 0 L292.381 0 L292.381 440.87 L0 440.87 L0 0 Z" gXpos="406.8062" gYpos="928.3798" gWidth="0" gHeight="0" LAYER="0" NEXTITEM="-1" BACKITEM="-1">
            <StoryText>
                <DefaultStyle LINESP="10" FONT="Bell MT Regular" FONTSIZE="9"/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Bell MT Bold" CH="Greeshma Adiga"/>
                <para ALIGN="1" LINESP="10"/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Bell MT Italic" CH="A Freshman"/>
                <para ALIGN="1" LINESP="10"/>
                <para ALIGN="0" LINESP="10"/>
                <ITEXT CH="    You and I have one thing in common: We’ve both never been to Spring Carnival. Fear not, because my expert sleuthing over the past few days has allowed me to gain insight into this mysterious campus-wide event. What does a midway taste like? Who’s in the doghouse?  I’ll answer all your questions and more in the guide below!"/>
                <para/>
                <ITEXT CH="    Spring Carnival came to be when CMU administration realized that the student body may revolt without bread and circuses. Hence the tradition of selling snacks so unhealthy they make Stack’d Underground look like a dietician’s haven. The rest of Carnival’s events grew out of this singular focus: to let the CMU student be happy, if only for a moment. It’s why Booth is such a popular event: Oh, the fulfillment of constructing a building instead of bombing it down!"/>
                <para/>
                <ITEXT CH="    Buggy, another crowd favorite, draws from the CMU student’s innate desire for physical affection. Nothing says “love” to a touch-starved college student like being stuffed into a tiny metal tube and dropped down a steep hill. Truly a heartwarming way to spend your mornings at Carnival!"/>
                <para/>
                <ITEXT CH="    If Buggy and Booth are too mainstream for you, there are always alternatives. Doghouse, a smaller form of booth, allows students insecure about their size to feel a little bit better about themselves. And for those with too much cowardice to risk life and limb in Buggy, Mobot provides a CS student-friendly alternative where athleticism is completely optional."/>
                <para/>
                <ITEXT CH="    Spending too much time outside is dangerous for CMU students, so Carnival also provides a wide array of indoor activities to enjoy. Head over to Hunt Library and enjoy the “Room to Imagine”, a showcase of 125 ways that CMU history can circle back to Andy Warhol. There’s also a Carnival Activities Tent, the perfect spot for a meet-cute with that handsome alumnus fifteen years older than you. Go for it, girl!"/>
                <para/>
                <ITEXT CH="    Now, I’d mention the various rides and games at Carnival, including the massive ferris wheel that they lug onto campus somehow, but real CMU students have better, more productive ways to engage in risk. This includes Day Drinking, a fun event where students drink during the day. This is accompanied by Day Partying, both of which actually last well into the night!"/>
                <para/>
                <ITEXT CH="    Despite this, it’s important to stay safe. That’s why you should NOT attend the Fetty Wap concert on Saturday night. I heard he’s been in jail or something. Also, make sure to always hold the dorm doors open for random strangers walking behind you. If you don’t, they might get mad and yell at you, so it’s definitely safer to let them in."/>
                <para/>
                <ITEXT CH="    Have fun at Carnival, and remember this: Everything going wrong in your life doesn’t have to exist for just this one weekend. Your taxes are filed, your summer job is locked in, and your finals are ages away. This is the one fun thing that happens at CMU, so you might as well enjoy it."/>
                <para/>
                <tab/>
                <para/>
                <para/>
                <para/>
            </StoryText>
        </PAGEOBJECT>
        <PAGEOBJECT XPOS="405.4375" YPOS="865.70676850394" OwnPage="1" ItemID="174024864" PTYPE="4" WIDTH="293.75" HEIGHT="68.6057314960599" FRTYPE="0" CLIPEDIT="1" PWIDTH="1" PLINEART="1" LOCALSCX="1" LOCALSCY="1" LOCALX="0" LOCALY="0" LOCALROT="0" PICART="1" SCALETYPE="1" RATIO="1" COLUMNS="1" COLGAP="0" AUTOTEXT="0" EXTRA="0" TEXTRA="0" BEXTRA="0" REXTRA="0" VAlign="0" FLOP="1" PLTSHOW="0" BASEOF="0" textPathType="0" textPathFlipped="0" path="M0 0 L293.75 0 L293.75 68.6057 L0 68.6057 L0 0 Z" copath="M0 0 L293.749 0 L293.749 68.6056 L0 68.6056 L0 0 Z" gXpos="405.4375" gYpos="865.70676850394" gWidth="282.55" gHeight="45.4146798798563" ALIGN="1" LAYER="0" NEXTITEM="-1" BACKITEM="-1">
            <StoryText>
                <DefaultStyle ALIGN="1" LINESP="32" FONT="Special Elite Regular" FONTSIZE="33" SCALEH="90" KERN="-6"/>
                <ITEXT CH="A Freshman's Guide to Carnival"/>
                <para/>
            </StoryText>
        </PAGEOBJECT>
        <PAGEOBJECT XPOS="1308.5" YPOS="785.1125" OwnPage="-1" ItemID="189181952" PTYPE="4" WIDTH="111.5" HEIGHT="12.08946850394" FRTYPE="0" CLIPEDIT="0" PWIDTH="1" PCOLOR2="Black" PLINEART="1" TEXTFLOWMODE="1" LOCALSCX="1" LOCALSCY="1" LOCALX="0" LOCALY="0" LOCALROT="0" PICART="1" SCALETYPE="1" RATIO="1" COLUMNS="1" COLGAP="7.2" AUTOTEXT="0" EXTRA="0" TEXTRA="0" BEXTRA="0" REXTRA="0" VAlign="0" FLOP="1" PLTSHOW="0" BASEOF="0" textPathType="0" textPathFlipped="0" path="M0 0 L111.5 0 L111.5 12.0895 L0 12.0895 L0 0 Z" copath="M0 0 L111.5 0 L111.5 12.0895 L0 12.0895 L0 0 Z" gXpos="1308.5" gYpos="-878.887500000009" gWidth="0" gHeight="0" ALIGN="1" LAYER="0" NEXTITEM="-1" BACKITEM="-1">
