        <PAGEOBJECT XPOS="-434.2633" YPOS="1863.8125" OwnPage="-1" ItemID="171195296" PTYPE="4" WIDTH="350.7375" HEIGHT="102.0375" FRTYPE="0" CLIPEDIT="1" PWIDTH="1" PLINEART="1" LOCALSCX="1" LOCALSCY="1" LOCALX="0" LOCALY="0" LOCALROT="0" PICART="1" SCALETYPE="1" RATIO="1" COLUMNS="1" COLGAP="0" AUTOTEXT="0" EXTRA="0" TEXTRA="0" BEXTRA="0" REXTRA="0" VAlign="0" FLOP="1" PLTSHOW="0" BASEOF="0" textPathType="0" textPathFlipped="0" path="M0 0 L350.737 0 L350.737 102.037 L0 102.037 L0 0 Z" copath="M0 0 L350.737 0 L350.737 102.037 L0 102.037 L0 0 Z" gXpos="-434.2633" gYpos="2695.8125" gWidth="282.55" gHeight="45.4146798798563" ALIGN="1" LAYER="0" NEXTITEM="-1" BACKITEM="-1">
            <StoryText>
                <DefaultStyle ALIGN="1" LINESP="28" FONT="Special Elite Regular" FONTSIZE="33" SCALEH="90" KERN="-10"/>
                <ITEXT SCALEH="90" KERN="-10" CH="BREAKING: CMU to join Division E"/>
                <trail LINESP="31"/>
            </StoryText>
        </PAGEOBJECT>
        <PAGEOBJECT XPOS="112.724392307692" YPOS="2232.86461538461" OwnPage="2" ItemID="171200960" PTYPE="4" WIDTH="353.712307692308" HEIGHT="234.08538461539" FRTYPE="0" CLIPEDIT="0" PWIDTH="1" PLINEART="1" LOCALSCX="1" LOCALSCY="1" LOCALX="0" LOCALY="0" LOCALROT="0" PICART="1" SCALETYPE="1" RATIO="1" COLUMNS="2" COLGAP="7.2" AUTOTEXT="0" EXTRA="0" TEXTRA="0" BEXTRA="0" REXTRA="0" VAlign="0" FLOP="1" PLTSHOW="0" BASEOF="0" textPathType="0" textPathFlipped="0" path="M0 0 L353.712 0 L353.712 234.085 L0 234.085 L0 0 Z" copath="M0 0 L353.712 0 L353.712 234.085 L0 234.085 L0 0 Z" gXpos="112.724392307692" gYpos="1400.8646153846" gWidth="0" gHeight="0" PSTYLE="Default Paragraph Style" LAYER="0" NEXTITEM="-1" BACKITEM="-1">
            <StoryText>
                <DefaultStyle PARENT="Default Paragraph Style" LINESP="10" FONT="Bell MT Regular" FONTSIZE="9" KERN="0" LANGUAGE="en_US"/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Bell MT Bold" FONTSIZE="9" CH="Jupiter"/>
                <para PARENT="Default Paragraph Style" ALIGN="1" LINESP="10"/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Bell MT Italic" FONTSIZE="9" KERN="0" CH="How do I get down from here? "/>
                <para PARENT="Default Paragraph Style" ALIGN="1" LINESP="10"/>
                <para/>
                <ITEXT CH="    As students, staff, and alumni flood the Midway this Carnival, they’ll notice the usual arrangement of booths, each with its own unique design. Navigating through the Midway, entranced with the artistry of Spring Carnival, they’ll walk slowly into the shadow lurking at the back of the Midway. There, they’ll find the newest addition to the Booth competition: Tall Booth."/>
                <para/>
                <ITEXT CH="    The point of Tall Booth is not simply to build a sound structure with a nice exterior. Instead, the simple objective of Tall booth is height. Build the tallest booth imaginable. How tall? To space and beyond ideally. "/>
                <para/>
                <ITEXT CH="    According to the committee responsible for founding Tall Booth, building one requires creative thinking. As such, builders are actually encouraged not to complete the usually mandated BioRaft training for building booths as such training prohibits the flow of ideas for extending the height of the booth. In observing the building of Tall Booths, reporters have noticed all manners of creative building methods. There were reporters on ladders stacked on ladders in order to reach the 9th or 10th stories of some booths. Or, 2 by 4s being used to cover the outside of booths after builders have run out of exterior ply. "/>
                <para/>
                <ITEXT CH="    Venturing inside these booths, many feature one singular ladder to access the various floors, much like the ladders mounted on the sides of wind turbines. Staring up, visitors of Tall Booths report seeing the structure sway side to side and groan under their own weight. Some argue that the constant movement of the booth interferes with playing the games. Tall Booth builders argue that it's part of the fun."/>
                <para/>
                <ITEXT CH="    So, as you venture out on the Midway this spring, consider stopping by these marvels of jank engineering and experience Tall Booth!"/>
                <para/>
                <para/>
                <para/>
            </StoryText>
        </PAGEOBJECT>
        <PAGEOBJECT XPOS="119.9992" YPOS="2967.75" OwnPage="3" ItemID="190754432" PTYPE="2" WIDTH="222.4391" HEIGHT="327.375" FRTYPE="0" CLIPEDIT="0" PWIDTH="1" PLINEART="1" LOCALSCX="0.0556760204081633" LOCALSCY="0.0556760204081633" LOCALX="0" LOCALY="0" LOCALROT="0" PICART="1" SCALETYPE="0" RATIO="1" Pagenumber="0" PFILE="5.7 images/CathyDildo.PNG" PRFILE="Embedded Display P3" IRENDER="0" EPROF="Embedded Display P3" path="M0 0 L222.439 0 L222.439 327.375 L0 327.375 L0 0 Z" copath="M0 0 L222.439 0 L222.439 327.375 L0 327.375 L0 0 Z" gXpos="119.9992" gYpos="1303.7436" gWidth="0" gHeight="0" LAYER="0" NEXTITEM="-1" BACKITEM="-1"/>
        <PAGEOBJECT XPOS="-418.8758" YPOS="1986.8512" OwnPage="-1" ItemID="196046320" PTYPE="4" WIDTH="351" HEIGHT="204.2488" FRTYPE="0" CLIPEDIT="0" PWIDTH="1" PLINEART="1" LOCALSCX="1" LOCALSCY="1" LOCALX="0" LOCALY="0" LOCALROT="0" PICART="1" SCALETYPE="1" RATIO="1" COLUMNS="1" COLGAP="7.2" AUTOTEXT="0" EXTRA="0" TEXTRA="0" BEXTRA="0" REXTRA="0" VAlign="0" FLOP="1" PLTSHOW="0" BASEOF="0" textPathType="0" textPathFlipped="0" path="M0 0 L351 0 L351 204.249 L0 204.249 L0 0 Z" copath="M0 0 L351 0 L351 204.249 L0 204.249 L0 0 Z" gXpos="-418.8758" gYpos="1154.84799999999" gWidth="0" gHeight="0" PSTYLE="Default Paragraph Style" LAYER="0" NEXTITEM="-1" BACKITEM="-1">
            <StoryText>
                <DefaultStyle PARENT="Default Paragraph Style" LINESP="10" FONT="Bell MT Regular" FONTSIZE="9" KERN="0" LANGUAGE="en_US"/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Bell MT Bold" FONTSIZE="9" CH="BJupiterr"/>
                <para PARENT="Default Paragraph Style" ALIGN="1" LINESP="10"/>
                <ITEXT FONT="Bell MT Italic" FONTSIZE="9" KERN="0" CH="Marching Band Sports Professional "/>
                <para PARENT="Default Paragraph Style" ALIGN="1" LINESP="10"/>
                <para PARENT="Default Paragraph Style" LINESP="10"/>
                <ITEXT CH="    It may be shocking, but did you know that recreational activities outside of hackathons and internship applications exist? Some choose to engage in activities know as “sports.” One of the more popular examples is American football, a game in which guys jump around, tackle each other, and make strange hand gestures when the referees do something they don’t like. "/>
                <para/>
                <ITEXT CH="    Until now, CMU has competed in the lowest division of college athletics, Division III. However, for this upcoming season, CMU will be amongst the pioneers of a whole new kind of college athletics: Division E. What sets Division E apart from other divisions you may ask? Well, Division E is composed entirely of the least athletic schools you can think of!"/>
                <para/>
                <ITEXT CH="    The athletes defining this new wave of college athletics are powered entirely by celsius and the rush of getting a Lockheed Martin interview. While their mile time might be double that of a Division I athlete, it does not mean that the games will be any less entertaining. What Division E lacks in sporting spectacle, they make for in fun and whimsical marching bands!"/>
                <para/>
                <ITEXT CH="    Each marching band, above all CMU’s incredible Kiltie Band, has their own unique quirks and traditions. You’ll often hear the Kilties shouting their infamous Anti-cheers to throw the other team off their rhythm or playing songs like Jaws to turn the tide of the game. So, this fall, come witness the newest addition to college athletics: Division Marching E!"/>
                <para/>
                <para/>
            </StoryText>
        </PAGEOBJECT>
